This project is a Coil port and adaptation of IR, with additional Coil code.
Its scalar type and opcode encodings, instruction layout, builder conventions,
constant folding, and call prototype format derive from IR. Its analysis,
allocation, and emission pipeline is developed with IR as the reference.
This is an incomplete implementation, not an upstream release or a claim of
full compatibility. Ported/adapted metadata and construction modules identify
upstream sources in their file headers. See docs/PROVENANCE.md for the source
map and implementation differences.

Upstream design acknowledgments (from ir.c):
- Cliff Click and Michael Paleczny, "A Simple Graph-Based Intermediate
  Representation", ACM SIGPLAN Workshop on Intermediate Representations,
  1995: the Sea-of-Nodes logical representation.
- Mike Pall, LuaJIT IR and "LuaJIT 2.0 intellectual property disclosure and
  research opportunities", November 2009: the compact physical representation.
  http://lua-users.org/lists/lua-l/2009-11/msg00089.html
IR's register allocator also cites Christian Wimmer's work on linear-scan
allocation, interval splitting, and allocation on SSA form; those references
remain relevant to this implementation's split-interval allocator.

TPDE / coil-tpde are additional references for the standalone-library/compiler-
backend separation and target/container implementation work. TPDE credits
Alexis Engelke and T0b1. No TPDE module is vendored or imported by this package.
Their Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception license is separate from IR's MIT license;
any future source adaptation must retain the applicable notices and license.
